			"date": "2023-02-15T22:36:17.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@bastianallgeier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>bastianallgeier</span></a></span> Long term: merits.<br>Short term: marketing.</p><p>Bash is still kicking. Vim is still kicking. Linux is still king of the hill for any serious development or industry. None had \"marketing\".</p><p>Coldfusion, ASP, Flash... dead and gone. Marketed well.</p>",
