				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/287/949/593/182/322/original/ea34d8a24964f103.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-15T22:44:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@bastianallgeier\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>bastianallgeier</span></a></span> Long term is whenever the marketing stopped paying for promotion.</p><p>Is the project still alive and popular once the marketing budeget is removed? It's a long term project.</p><p>Still needs marketing? It's a short term project reliant on the money drip to succeed. The moment that goes, the project dies. That's a short term success.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
