			},
			"date": "2023-02-18T12:15:46.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Long = the glacial rate of my replies? 😅 I'm thinking years. I have 11ty in mind - I'm not saying possums aren't great marketing... I *tend* to associate software carefully developed over a longer term with quality and reliability, which increases adoption and success in the long term. I think marketing and hype can help adoption in the short term but if the quality isn't there, the success won't last. IMHO.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
